; regression test for a real retrofit gap missed when numbers.kurt was first labelled for the
; `local`/export feature (doc/kurt-soundness.md #7): `^` (power) had `infix ^ 75 75` declared
; but every axiom that mentioned it was commented out ("laws of exponents", left disabled),
; so nothing exported ever needed `^` -- meaning `^`'s own syntax silently stopped surviving
; `load numbers`, exactly like `!` (factorial) did before `numbers.kurt` got a `0! = 1`-style fix.
; Confirmed the break directly: `2 ^ 3` parsed as bare space-application (`[2, ^, 3]`, not an
; infix expression) after `load numbers`, so `calc on` never saw an operator to compute.
; Fixed by adding a genuine, unconditionally-true axiom (`$a ^ 1 = $a`, chosen over
; `$a ^ 0 = 1` specifically to avoid the 0^0-undefined edge case) that actually mentions `^`,
; so its syntax is now part of the exported closure -- confirmed here via `calc on` actually
; computing `2 ^ 3` (impossible if `^` were still parsed as a bare space-applied symbol).
load numbers
calc on
2 ^ 3 = 8
